# `railway up` uploads the working tree minus .gitignore and this file. The Dockerfile needs only
# requirements-ui.txt, .streamlit/, ops/, rag/, cases/, runs/r2-final/, runs/live-final-2/, three files of
# engine/out/, agent/__init__.py + agent/security.py, schema_engine/ (attestation.py) and ui/, so skip the bulk
# (data/ and graph/ alone are over 150 MB). Exclusions only: a `!` line here overrides .gitignore
# and could upload .env or local runs.
.env
.env.*
.claude/
data/
graph/
docs/
# agent/ minus the two stdlib-only files the image copies (tracked source; a parent dir excluded with `agent/`
# could not be re-included)
agent/*
!agent/__init__.py
!agent/security.py
# engine/out/ stays (about 1.5 MB): the UI reads its detector backtest, containment summary and proof snapshot
engine/*.py
engine/__pycache__/
etl/
mcp/
qa/
contracts/
policy/
tests/
IMPLEMENTATION.md
PLAN.md
